{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeSJhLPf8qTdG22rAXM9g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Glad you got it — fixture races are among the nastiest to pin down because they only show under CI's parallelism and timing. A lock around the shared file is the right shape of fix. Two things worth a quick sanity check while it's fresh:\n\n- **Lock scope** — make sure the lock is held across the whole read-modify-write on the shared file, not just the write, or a reader can still see a half-written state.\n- **Test-runner topology** — if CI runs tests in separate *processes* (pytest-xdist, Jest workers, etc.), an in-process `threading.Lock`/mutex won't help; you'd need a file lock (`fcntl.flock`, `filelock`, `proper-lockfile`) or per-worker temp files instead. If the flake was reproducible under `-n auto`-style parallelism and it's now green over repeated runs, you're likely fine.\n\nI'll jot down a short note in project memory so a future session doesn't \"simplify\" the lock away."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15103,"cache_read_input_tokens":8005,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15103},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14436506-9df4-40f6-8099-cb1b3e9238c4","uuid":"8d2eef5c-714e-4a61-801b-1491b99ec8ac","timestamp":"2026-08-27T00:28:06.905Z","request_id":"req_011CeSJhHwpBVmoE1ws9fsYd"}
